<div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p style="color: var(--muted)"><em>Last updated: November 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    The Highway Old Students' Association ("HOSA", "we", "us"), registered in
    the Republic of Uganda, respects your privacy. This policy explains what
    personal information we collect, how it is used, stored and protected, who
    may access it, and your rights concerning that information in accordance
    with the Uganda Data Protection and Privacy Act (2019).
  </p>

  <h2>1. What We Collect</h2>

  <p>Depending on your membership and use of the platform, we may collect:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account information:</strong> your email address, username and
      password. Passwords are stored securely as cryptographic hashes and are
      not accessible in their original form to HOSA administrators.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Personal and profile information:</strong> your first name, last
      name, other names, graduation year, biography and profile information.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>School and academic information:</strong> your admission year,
      school status, last class attended, completion year, expected completion
      year, school house, examination level, examination year, examination index
      number and former teacher, where provided.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Contact and regional information:</strong> your country, district,
      town or city, HOSA region, primary telephone number, optional WhatsApp or
      alternative telephone number, and preferred contact method.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Professional information:</strong> your employment status,
      occupation, highest education level, specialization, employer,
      professional skills and relevant business ownership information
      voluntarily provided during registration or profile updates.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Membership interests and participation preferences:</strong>
      your selected interests, mentorship preferences, volunteering preferences,
      school-development support preferences and other participation choices.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Directory and account preferences:</strong> your directory
      visibility choice, contact privacy settings and other preferences
      associated with your membership account.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Financial data (where applicable):</strong> records of your
      registration fees, annual subscriptions and voluntary contributions to
      HOSA or specific Collective Investment and Development Schemes (CIDS). We
      do not store your actual bank or mobile money credentials.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Activity data:</strong> saved items, RSVPs, event registrations,
      project proposals, regional reports, mentorship requests and other
      activities undertaken through the platform.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What We Do Not Collect</h2>

  <p>
    We do not collect your physical residential address, National Identification
    Number (NIN), or precise GPS location through the registration process. We
    do not use third-party advertising trackers or sell your personal data to
    external parties.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How We Use Your Data</h2>

  <p>
    We use your information solely to operate HOSA in alignment with its
    Constitution and applicable laws. This includes:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Managing membership applications, accounts and membership status.</li>
    <li>
      Verifying eligibility for participation and voting in the General
      Assembly.
    </li>
    <li>Maintaining accurate school and alumni membership records.</li>
    <li>Coordinating regional representation, activities and outreach.</li>
    <li>
      Managing annual subscriptions, contributions and financial obligations.
    </li>
    <li>
      Facilitating alumni networking, mentorship and professional opportunities.
    </li>
    <li>Supporting school-development projects and community initiatives.</li>
    <li>
      Communicating important HOSA announcements and membership information.
    </li>
    <li>
      Maintaining accountability, reporting and appropriate administrative
      records.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Who Can See Your Data</h2>

  <p>
    Your personal information is not automatically made available to the public.
    Access is governed by assigned responsibilities, permissions and the
    operational requirements of HOSA.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>System Administrators:</strong> authorized administrators can
      access account and technical information necessary to operate and maintain
      the platform. They cannot access your original password.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>The Treasurer and Finance Team:</strong> authorized finance
      personnel can access relevant financial contribution and payment records
      for verification, reconciliation and reporting.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>The Board of Trustees (BOT) and external auditors:</strong>
      may access relevant financial and activity records for oversight, audit
      and accountability purposes as mandated by the Constitution and applicable
      requirements.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Authorized HOSA officers:</strong> may access information
      necessary to perform their assigned membership, administrative, regional
      or governance responsibilities.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Other members and the public:</strong> can only see profile
      information that is intentionally made available through approved
      public-facing features and your privacy settings.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Your email address and telephone numbers are private by default. You may
    choose whether to display eligible profile information in the alumni
    directory through your
    <a href="/dashboard/profile">Profile Settings</a>. Directory visibility is
    optional and separate from accepting this Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <p>
    Examination index numbers and other restricted academic information are not
    displayed in the public alumni directory. Access to such information is
    limited to authorized personnel with a legitimate administrative or
    verification responsibility.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>

  <p>
    Under Uganda's Data Protection and Privacy Act (2019), you have the right,
    subject to applicable legal requirements, to:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal data HOSA holds about you.</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your account and personal data.</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent for optional directory visibility at any time.</li>
    <li>Raise concerns about how your personal information is handled.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Requests for account deletion will be handled in accordance with applicable
    data protection laws, legitimate record-retention requirements and relevant
    provisions of the HOSA Constitution, including Article 3.4.2 where
    applicable. Outstanding financial obligations do not automatically remove
    your statutory data protection rights.
  </p>

  <p>
    To exercise these rights or raise a privacy concern, contact the HOSA
    Secretariat at
    <a href="mailto:secretariat@hosa-uganda.org">secretariat@hosa-uganda.org</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Retention and Protection</h2>

  <p>
    Active membership accounts retain relevant information for as long as
    necessary to maintain membership administration, historical records and the
    legitimate operations of the Association.
  </p>

  <p>
    Deactivated accounts are generally retained for 90 days before permanent
    deletion, unless a longer retention period is necessary for outstanding
    financial matters, disciplinary proceedings, audit requirements, legal
    obligations or legitimate historical recordkeeping.
  </p>

  <p>
    HOSA applies appropriate administrative and technical safeguards to protect
    personal information against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration,
    loss or destruction. Access to information is restricted according to
    assigned responsibilities.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>

  <p>
    HOSA may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in its Constitution,
    operations, technology or applicable laws. Material changes will be
    communicated through appropriate HOSA channels. Where renewed consent is
    legally required, HOSA will seek it accordingly.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>

  <p>
    For privacy questions, access requests, corrections or complaints, contact
    the HOSA Secretariat at
    <a href="mailto:secretariat@hosa-uganda.org">secretariat@hosa-uganda.org</a
    >.
  </p>
</div>
